{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 105, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct input-output edge with a conv gives large gains, unlike replacing skip, pool or 1x1."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With the direct edge missing and edge 0 only a skip, the edit hurt strongly, especially on ImageNet16."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 when edge 3 is none nearly disconnects the cell and costs far more than usual."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with a conv gains more than replacing a 1x1 conv, which is already similar."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the direct edge, a skip on edge 5 helps gradient flow and gains on all datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op with a conv gives gains, whereas replacing a 3x3 conv with 1x1 does not."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 1 compensates for the missing direct edge and gave +10 on ImageNet16."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Downsizing edge 4 hurts less when edge 3 is none, with strong gains on C10 and ImageNet16."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 missing, a cheaper conv on edge 2 is beneficial on all three datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none